Z||000003||Voytek||12-05-2001||03:04 PM||||It's all tied in together, i.e. it's all grounded.  I had a grounding problem in my fusebox one time and the radio would die periodically.  I couldn't figure out why.<P>I would suggest just drying everything (unplug the connectors, etc.) and then see if it's still smoking.<P>I washed my engine one time ('87 GT V6) and the ignition coil got fried (the other little cube by the distributor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).  The car died about 2 km from my house.  Now, if I ever wash the engine, I make sure EVERYTHING is dry first.<P>Powodzenia.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Rodrv6||12-05-2001||04:11 PM||||The cruise solenoid and the radio memory share the same fuse.  Like above, try drying it out and see if it's okay.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
